    <string name="lab_flex_help_apps_body">By default, only apps that support Flex mode, like YouTube, Camera, and Gallery, split the screen top and bottom. Other apps don\'t change. To split other apps too, set them to \'Flex mode\' in \'%1$s\'. For video apps without their own controls, choose \'GOAT panel\'.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_apps_title">6. How apps differ</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_nod_body">With this on, you can toggle Flex mode by folding the fully unfolded phone slightly to 130–160° and unfolding it again within 3 s (a \'nod\'). While Flex mode is on, it stays on even when unfolded. It turns off when you close the phone or turn off the screen.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_nod_title">5. Toggle Flex mode with a nod</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_off_body">Turn off the top switch to restore the settings and fold state GOAT changed. Restarting also restores them.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_off_title">7. Turn off and restore</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_range_body">Drag the gauge\'s two handles to set the range. Long-press a handle to adjust by 1°. Tap [%1$s] to try it right away.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_range_title">4. Set the angle range</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_shizuku_body">Switching to Flex mode requires Shizuku. See \'Permission setup\' in the three-dot menu for how to connect. Once connected, you can turn on the top switch.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_shizuku_title">2. Connect Shizuku first</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_use_body">Turn on the top switch, then slowly fold the unfolded phone in portrait. When the angle enters the set range, Flex mode turns on with a vibration, and the normal screen returns when it leaves the range. Once Flex mode is on, tilting or rotating the phone won\'t turn it off. It doesn\'t turn on if you fold in landscape.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_use_title">3. Turn on and use</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_help_what_body">The Fold8 doesn\'t switch to Flex mode even when half-folded and standing. With this on, GOAT switches to Flex mode when you fold the phone in portrait into the angle range you set. The app you were using shows on the top half, and a control panel on the bottom half.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_panel_ambient">Ambient</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_panel_ambient_body">Screen analysis captures the top half at a small size and extracts colors on the device only. Captured images are never saved or sent. Protected video, like Netflix, uses the poster or app color instead.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_panel_body">Apps set to \'GOAT panel\' show a control panel on the bottom half when half-folded. Use it for apps without their own controls, like Netflix and Disney+.</string>
    <string name="lab_flex_panel_button_blur">Button Glass Blur</string>
