    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_limits_body">Android 11 removed the setting that made the whole system full screen. GOAT hides the status bar by placing a small invisible window in front of the screen, so by design the status bar still shows in these cases:\n• While using the keyboard: hidden again when you close the keyboard.\n• Screens that don\'t allow display over other apps, like Settings or permission dialogs: hidden again when you leave that screen.\nIf it still shows, tap [Hide Again] in the notification.</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_limits_title">6. Limits on Android 11 and later</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_permission_body">Needs the Modify system settings permission, same as Advanced screen scaling. See \'Permission setup\' in the three-dot menu for how to grant it. Changing the mic and camera use indicator also requires Shizuku.</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_permission_title">2. Required permission</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_statusbar_body">Hides the entire status bar so apps can use that area. Swiping down from the top edge or going back shows it briefly, then it hides again. Needs the \'Display over other apps\' permission. If Shizuku is connected, GOAT grants it for you.</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_statusbar_title">5. Hide status bar</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_unhidable_body">Some icons can\'t be hidden because their internal names differ across One UI versions. The mic and camera use indicator (green dot) can only be changed on Android 13 and earlier. On Android 14 and later the system blocks the change, so the switch is locked.</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_unhidable_title">3. Icons that can\'t be hidden</string>
    <string name="lab_status_icons_help_what_body">Hides the status bar icons you pick, such as alarm, Bluetooth, and vibrate. Only the icons are hidden. The features keep working.</string>
